# b01c06 scene chunks — /and-substance chapter b01c06 Phase 2+3 draft
# Authored: 2026-05-30
# Schema: schemas/showrunner-memory.schema.md (scenes[] block)
# Chapter: b01c06 — "a request becomes a precedent"
# Replaces planned chunk in memory (named-person ward-elder delivery + brief Wren encounter)
# with new chapter concept per task brief: Wren's ask + directed feed + first self-authored exception.
#
# Chapter substance_delta (from task brief — to be rolled up across scenes):
#   axes_in_motion:
#     - moral_framework:         direction: down, target_delta_magnitude: 1.0, anchor: cl06a
#     - social_tether-prot-rise: direction: up,   target_delta_magnitude: 1.0, anchor: cl06b
#     - capability:              direction: up,    target_delta_magnitude: 1.0, anchor: cl06a
#   axes_held:
#     - position-prot-rise        (no new formalization event)
#     - relational_anchor_status  (Wren contact is the tether move, not anchor-weight move)
#     - moral_legibility_to_self  (the recording is honest; crack does not deepen here)
#     - political_register-prot   (no court-tier feed content this chapter)
#
# Roll-up arithmetic — per-scene allocation:
#   s01: social_tether-prot-rise +1.0  (first spoken exchange; Wren asks, Taylor answers in words)
#   s02: capability +1.0, moral_framework -0.5  (yes + directed feed; girl found)
#   s03: moral_framework -0.5  (recording the exception; the prohibition authored, not merely permitted)
#   TOTAL: moral_framework -1.0 EXACT; social_tether-prot-rise +1.0 EXACT; capability +1.0 EXACT ✓

---

# Note on new cost_ledger entries required (not yet in memory):
#   cl06a:
#     gain: "capability +1 | moral_framework -1" (same event: directed reading at Wren's ask)
#     cost: "opportunity-missed: the prohibition now has an author-sanctioned exception on the books —
#             Taylor wrote it herself, for a good reason, in clean daylight; the road's first paving-stone
#             laid gently; the next exception will reference this one"
#     anchor: { book: b01, chapter: b01c06, scene: null }
#   cl06b:
#     gain: "social_tether-prot-rise +1"
#     cost: "journey-required: cl06a (same Wren-ask event; tether deepening is the other face of the
#             spoken exchange — Wren is now a person Taylor has answered in words, not a ward-in-coverage)"
#     anchor: { book: b01, chapter: b01c06, scene: b01c06s01 }
#
# These entries should be appended to series.substance.cost_ledger[] at /and-substance chapter Phase 6 persist.

---

scenes:
  - slug: b01c06s01
    chunk: |
      [force: Taylor's ward-coverage discipline — reading the Hook's morning as she has read
      every Hook morning; bodies, junction-traffic, the particular stillness of a stitch-house
      in the pre-work hour before the thread gets threaded]. She is at the drain-angle near
      Butcher's Lane when [event: Wren finds Taylor and addresses her directly, the first spoken
      exchange between them]. Not a summons. Not a greeting. Wren steps in front of her in the
      lane with the particular body-carriage of someone who has been composing what to say and
      has decided to say it now.

      [image: Wren — hands at her sides, not fidgeting; the stitch-maker's ward stillness that is
      attentiveness holding itself still, not nerves; the peripheral-tracking eyes that Taylor has
      read in the insect-feed before now seeing Taylor directly for the first time with something
      specific to say]. Wren says: there is a girl who comes to the stitch-house for trim-work,
      a day-labor child from the lower lane. She has not come in three days. The stitch-maker will
      not note it; ward-children who miss work get replaced, not searched for. Wren has no standing
      to search. She has no coin. But she has noticed the foreign woman can find things. [mechanism:
      Wren's ask in plain Flea Bottom form — she names the girl ("Liss, she's nine, she does the
      trim-ends on the same form I use"), the last-seen location (the lower lane junction, morning
      before last), the absence-duration (three days), and then stops; she does not add anything;
      she does not explain what she wants done with the finding].

      [force: the ask's specific moral weight — small, named, clean; no faction logic; no patron
      backing; a child who stops coming to work is either moved on or in trouble, and both are
      findable with the architecture Taylor runs; the ask does not cost the prohibition anything
      except the prohibition itself]. [event: Taylor goes still in the lane]. The feed is already
      running; the stitch-house is in range; the lane junction is in range; she has been reading
      both since this morning without finding anything anomalous. She has not run the feed at a
      named person. She has run the feed at the ward. The distinction is one she has held since
      b01c01. [force: the ask's refusal-terms — if she says no, she says no to a child, for a
      reason she cannot name to Wren, for a prohibition whose explanation would require an
      accounting she has not given to anyone]. She looks at Wren's hands. They are held still.
      Not requesting anything beyond what was said.

      [event: Taylor answers Wren in words — the first spoken exchange; she says she will look].
      She does not say how. [event: social_tether-prot-rise: Wren moves from ward-in-coverage to
      person-who-asked-and-was-answered; cl06b gain side; the tether deepens through the spoken
      exchange itself, not through any operational consequence]. Wren nods once — the economical
      acknowledgment of someone who asked something real and got a real answer — and turns back
      toward the stitch-house lane.

    substance_delta:
      axes_in_motion:
        - axis: social_tether-prot-rise
          direction: up
          target_delta_magnitude: 1.0
          cost_ledger_anchor: cl06b
          notes: "first spoken Wren-Taylor exchange; Wren names the ask, Taylor answers in words;
                  ward-in-coverage becomes person-who-asked-and-was-answered; the tether deepens
                  not through network architecture but through the spoken response; cl06b gain side.
                  This is the scene that must carry the dialogue-cobonded anchor — /and-write must
                  treat the Wren ask and Taylor answer as dialogue-anchor bones with [wren-stitch-maker-flea-bottom-ward:N]
                  and [taylor-hebert-kl-122ac:N] citations."
      axes_held:
        - axis: moral_framework
          rationale: "Taylor has not said yes to the directed reading yet — she has said she will look,
                      which is engagement but not the crossing; the prohibition is still the operative
                      fence at scene-close; the decision is made but the act is not yet performed"
        - axis: capability
          rationale: "no feed deployment yet; Taylor is processing the ask; capability moves in s02
                      when the feed is pointed at a named person"
        - axis: relational_anchor_status
          rationale: "the spoken exchange deepens the tether (social_tether-prot-rise) but does not
                      yet add operational weight to the anchor (that would require Wren entering a
                      protection calculus); anchor holds at rank 2 through scene-close"
        - axis: political_register-prot
          rationale: "no court-tier content; the exchange is ward-layer, child-register; resentment
                      has no material to form on in this scene"
        - axis: moral_legibility_to_self
          rationale: "Taylor's accounting has not run yet on what she is about to do; self-accounting
                      runs after the act, not before; legibility holds"
      density_target: 0.6-0.75

    scene_conflict:
      protagonist_force: "Taylor's discipline of ward-reading as coverage-not-targeting — she has
                          run the feed at the ward, never at a named person; Wren's ask is the first
                          time the distinction has been handed to her as a question rather than a rule"
      opposing_force: "the ask's specific moral cleanness — small, named, helpable; the child is
                       nine, the absence is three days, Wren has no standing to search; the
                       prohibition's refusal would require an accounting Taylor cannot give to Wren
                       without naming what the architecture is"
      stakes_axis: social_tether-prot-rise
    stale_since: null


  - slug: b01c06s02
    chunk: |
      She does not go back to the drain-angle. [force: Taylor's operational discipline — she runs
      the find in the same ward-walk register she uses for coverage maintenance; nothing about her
      movement announces a search]. [event: Taylor points the insect-feed at a named person for
      the first time at another's explicit request — the directed reading begins]. The feed opens
      on the lower lane junction, widens to the three connecting courts, begins the kind of
      body-differential read she has only ever run on classes of bodies — the sick, the
      agitated, the moving-against-pattern — now run on a specific body by name. Liss.
      [image: the feed narrowing to a child-sized signature — nine years old, trim-work calluses,
      the particular body-chemistry of someone who does close sewing work; distinguishable in the
      feed as a type, not yet found as an individual]. She runs the lower lane. She runs the
      three courts. The stitch-house is in the north court; she reads it without finding the
      girl's signature in it.

      [mechanism: the directed reading as a new class of feed-deployment — not coverage-maintenance
      (ambient, ward-wide) but targeting (specific body, specific name, active search); the
      feed has been running the ward for four months and Taylor has never pointed it at a person;
      she is pointing it now, at Wren's ask, and the distinction between reading-the-ward and
      reading-a-person-in-the-ward is one she is crossing in the act of looking]. Two courts
      clear. She extends to the adjacent ward. The feed opens on Tickler's Lane and its
      tributaries — a ward she has mapped but not covered as densely. [event: Taylor finds the
      girl — Liss is in a room off Tickler's Lane, alive, with three other children and an adult
      woman who reads in the feed as a kin-signature, not a threat-signature; the girl has gone to
      a cousin two wards over]. The find takes less than an hour. The feed returns the girl
      upright and in shelter. Taylor reads: alive. Present. Not in danger.

      [force: the relief that arrives before the accounting — the girl is found, the ask is
      answered, and what arrives first in Taylor's chest is the particular quality of a good
      outcome before the ledger opens on how the outcome was produced]. [event: capability
      +1.0 — directed reading at a named person's request; the feed pointed, not ambient;
      cl06a gain side]. The accounting begins now, but it begins in the aftermath of already
      knowing the girl is alive. [force: the moral_framework breach completing in the act of
      having-done-it — the prohibition's first directed exception is behind Taylor; she cannot
      un-have-pointed-the-feed]. [event: moral_framework -0.5 — the directed reading is the
      crossing; cl06a cost side partial]. The feed resolves: Liss, alive, with a cousin in the
      lane two wards over. The result is clean. The architecture worked exactly as it should.

    substance_delta:
      axes_in_motion:
        - axis: capability
          direction: up
          target_delta_magnitude: 1.0
          cost_ledger_anchor: cl06a
          notes: "directed reading at a named person's request; feed pointed at a specific body
                  rather than run at ambient ward-coverage; this is the first targeting deployment
                  (as distinct from coverage-maintenance); cl06a gain side"
        - axis: moral_framework
          direction: down
          target_delta_magnitude: 0.5
          cost_ledger_anchor: cl06a
          notes: "the directed reading is the crossing — the prohibition's first directed exception
                  performed and completed; the breach is not rationalized away mid-scene, it arrives
                  as fact; cl06a cost side partial (remaining -0.5 lands in s03 when Taylor records
                  and authors the exception)"
      axes_held:
        - axis: social_tether-prot-rise
          rationale: "the tether move happened in s01 (spoken exchange); the find itself does not
                      further deepen the tether — it is operational consequence, not relational event"
        - axis: relational_anchor_status
          rationale: "Wren is not present in this scene; the find is about Liss; Wren does not
                      enter Taylor's protection calculus here; anchor holds at rank 2"
        - axis: political_register-prot
          rationale: "the find is ward-layer, child-register; no court-tier content; resentment
                      has no material to form on"
        - axis: moral_legibility_to_self
          rationale: "the accounting begins but does not complete in this scene — the recognition
                      that the exception has been authored lands in s03; legibility holds at s02-close"
        - axis: position-prot-rise
          rationale: "the find is between Taylor and Wren; no patron-tier visibility; no position event"
      density_target: 0.65-0.8

    scene_conflict:
      protagonist_force: "Taylor running the directed read with the same operational precision she
                          runs coverage-maintenance — the discipline that makes the find successful
                          is the same discipline that makes it a breach; the architecture works"
      opposing_force: "the distinction between reading-the-ward and reading-a-person-in-the-ward
                       — the prohibition's line is the line she crosses in the act of looking for
                       Liss; the opposition is not external pressure but the rule she set herself,
                       meeting the act she chose to perform"
      stakes_axis: moral_framework
    stale_since: null


  - slug: b01c06s03
    chunk: |
      She sends word the way she sends any ward-level message — through no channel that belongs
      to Jarvis, through no route that touches the arrangement. [event: Taylor returns the
      finding to Wren — she finds Wren at the stitch-house lane, tells her where the girl is,
      names the cousin and the lane]. The exchange takes thirty seconds. Wren takes the
      information with the same economy she brought to the ask — receives it, nods, does not
      add anything. [image: Wren's face at receipt — the specific quality of a child who asked
      something real and is getting a real answer; not gratitude-performance, just the expression
      of a person who can now act on what they needed to know]. She goes. Taylor watches her
      go. [force: the relief completing — the girl is alive, the ask is answered, Wren now
      knows where to look; the architecture delivered exactly what it was asked to deliver and
      the outcome is clean].

      [force: the accounting that follows the relief — Taylor's ledger opens on the directed
      reading now that there is no operational frame to hold it at a managed distance]. She
      runs the accounting explicitly and in order. First: the ask was clean. It was a child,
      a named person, a specific fear, and no faction logic anywhere in it. The ask was the
      cleanest she has received since arriving in King's Landing. Second: she said yes. Third:
      she pointed the feed at a named person for the first time in four months of running
      coverage, in the first time since arriving in this city. Fourth: the girl is alive.
      The outcome is good. Fifth: this happened. [event: Taylor records the exception in her
      internal ledger — she writes the accounting herself, in her own register, in the specific
      form of a ledger entry she is choosing to make rather than receiving as a conclusion].

      [mechanism: the difference between this exception and the prior ones — the Jarvis
      deliveries were rationalizations arrived at under pressure, accounting that needed
      Sera's weight on the other side of the balance to close; this one was authored without
      pressure, chosen in daylight, for a reason she still believes was good; and the specific
      weight of that is that she cannot claim duress; the exception was hers to write; she
      wrote it]. [event: moral_framework -0.5 — the recording of the exception completes the
      breach; what was a crossing in s02 becomes a precedent in s03; cl06a cost side completes].
      She does not sit with this. She does not not-sit with it. She records it: first directed
      reading at a named person's request. Ask clean. Outcome clean. Exception authored.
      [image: the ledger entry with no clause about regret — it names what happened, it names
      the reason, it names the result; the absence of regret is not absence of recognition;
      she knows what she has written; she has written it anyway; the road's first paving-stone,
      laid gently, with the best of intentions, at no one's demand but her own].

    substance_delta:
      axes_in_motion:
        - axis: moral_framework
          direction: down
          target_delta_magnitude: 0.5
          cost_ledger_anchor: cl06a
          notes: "Taylor records the exception in her own ledger, in her own words, without duress —
                  the crossing (s02) becomes a precedent (s03) in the act of authoring rather than
                  merely permitting; cl06a cost side completes; the road's first paving-stone is now
                  on the books with Taylor's hand on it"
      axes_held:
        - axis: social_tether-prot-rise
          rationale: "tether move completed in s01; s03 is aftermath and recording; no new relational
                      event with Wren deepens the tether further at scene level"
        - axis: capability
          rationale: "capability moved in s02; the ledger entry is accounting for what was done,
                      not a new deployment"
        - axis: relational_anchor_status
          rationale: "Wren receives the information and goes; no protection calculus is opened for
                      Wren in this scene; the ledger entry does not include Wren's name in any
                      deliverable accessible to Jarvis; anchor holds at rank 2 through chapter close"
        - axis: moral_legibility_to_self
          rationale: "Taylor's accounting is honest and complete — she knows what she did; but the
                      recognition does not crack deeper here than the chapter contract requires; she
                      records and continues; legibility holds at its entry rank (not a recognition-
                      suppression event; the recognition runs clean and gets filed as information)"
        - axis: political_register-prot
          rationale: "the find and the recording are ward-layer, no court-tier content; resentment
                      has no material here"
        - axis: position-prot-rise
          rationale: "the exception is between Taylor and Wren; nothing reaches the patron-tier;
                      position holds"
      density_target: 0.65-0.8

    scene_conflict:
      protagonist_force: "the accounting that must be run — Taylor does not avoid the ledger; she
                          opens it on the directed reading after the outcome is known, runs it
                          explicitly, and authors the exception entry herself; the discipline that
                          makes her honest makes the breach legible"
      opposing_force: "the good outcome — the girl is alive, the ask was clean, Wren's face at
                       receipt; the relief is real; the good outcome is what makes the accounting
                       unrefusable and the exception unreturnable; there is no clause to void the
                       entry on grounds that the result justified the crossing, because the crossing
                       is already in the ledger and the result does not change the entry"
      stakes_axis: moral_framework
    stale_since: null

